1
00:00:00,137 --> 00:00:02,227
(Sheldon:)Oh, glare.

2
00:00:02,640 --> 00:00:03,770
(Penny:)But on the other hand...

3
00:00:03,933 --> 00:00:07,433
(Penny:)...if things don't go well with Leonard,
I risk losing a really good friend.

4
00:00:07,603 --> 00:00:09,353
I mean, he's not looking for a fling.

5
00:00:09,522 --> 00:00:13,482
He's the kind that gets into a relationship
for, like you would say, light-years.

6
00:00:13,651 --> 00:00:14,781
(Sheldon:)I would not say that.

7
00:00:15,945 --> 00:00:19,575
No one would say that.
A light-year is a unit of distance, not time.

8
00:00:19,740 --> 00:00:21,780
(Penny:)Thank you for the clarification.

9
00:00:28,875 --> 00:00:30,585
(Sheldon:)Draft.

10
00:00:31,127 --> 00:00:34,337
You see, people hear the word "year"
and they think duration.

11
00:00:34,505 --> 00:00:38,045
Foot-pound has the same problem.
That's a unit of work, not of weight.

12
00:00:38,217 --> 00:00:39,387
(Penny:)Right. Thanks.

13
00:00:39,552 --> 00:00:43,012
- It's a common mistake.
- Not the first one I've made today.

14
00:00:43,472 --> 00:00:44,722
(Sheldon:)Okay.

15
00:00:45,516 --> 00:00:48,016
(Sheldon:)I think this will be my seat.

16
00:00:48,394 --> 00:00:50,854
(Penny:)Do you have anything to say
that has anything to do...

17
00:00:51,022 --> 00:00:53,062
(Penny:)...with, you know,
what I'm talking about?

18
00:00:53,816 --> 00:00:56,026
(Sheldon:)Well, let's see.

